    "result_text": "All done. The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern (a create-time snapshot stored on the owner).\n\n**Change:** `capacityWarning` is `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners at creation time (approaching the capacity limit of 50); the hard rejection at 50 (`CityAtCapacityException`) is unchanged.\n\nFiles modified:\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`capacity_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40`, a `computeCapacityWarning(owner)` method (counts city members case-insensitively, excluding the owner being saved, and returns `count >= 40 && count < 50`), and wired it into the create branch of `saveOwner` right after the bulk-signup warning.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` mapping + `formatCapacityWarning` helper (null stored value \u2192 explicit `false`).\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the owner schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it).\n- **`resources/db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n\nThe counting deliberately matches `assertCityHasCapacity` (same case-insensitive, exclude-self logic), so the warning band sits exactly below the hard limit. `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
